<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:  n1. The business activity of the Group falls within a single primary business segment viz ‘Investments &amp; Lending activities’ and hence there is no other reportable segment as per Ind AS 108 ‘operating segments’.  nt  n2. COVID - 19 pandemic has caused serious disruption on the global economic and business environment.  There is a huge uncertainty with regard  to its impact which cannot be reasonably determined at this stage.  However, the group has evaluated and considered to the extent possible the likely impact that may arise from COVID-19 pandemic as well as all event and circumstances upto the date of approval of these Financial results on the carrying value of its assets and liabilities as on 31.3.2020.  Based on the current indicators of future economic conditions, the group estimates to recover the  carrying amount of these assets  and adequate liquidity is available. These estimates are subject to uncertainty and may be affected by the severity and duration of the pandemic. The Group is continuously monitoring any material changes in future economic conditions.  n  n3. The Group has adopted Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS) notified by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA), with transition date April 1, 2018. Accordingly, the financial results for the Year Ended March 31, 2020 and March 31, 2019 are Ind AS compliant. ttttt  n  n4. The reconciliation of profit after tax as previously reported on account of transition from previous Indian GAAP to Ind AS are given as under:  n  nConsolidated tt  nYear ended 31st March, 2019 tt  nProfit after tax as reported under previous GAAP Rs. 2,200 Lakh tt  nAdjustment for ttttt  nFair valuation of oriented Mutual Funds  (net of tax) Rs. 166 Lakht  nDerecognisation of gain on sale of investments fair valued through other comprehensive income Rs. (317) Lakh  nTax Effect on the above Adjustments Rs. (49) Lakht  nTransferred to non controlling interest Rs. (1) Lakhtt  nProfit after tax for the period under Ind AS Rs. 1,999 Lakh tt  nInvestment fair value through other comprehensive income Rs.  (3,398)t Lakh  nTotal Comprehensive Income for the period under Ind AS Rs.  (1,398) Lakhtt  ntttttt  n5. Reconciliation of Equity and Other Equity as per previously reported on account of transition from previous Indian GAAP to Ind-AS is as follows :  nConsolidated tt  nAs at 31 March, 2019 and As at 1 April, 2018 t  nEquity as reported under previous GAAP and Ind AS Rs.  1,061 Lakh and Rs.  1,061 Lakht  nOther equity as reported under previous GAAP Rs. 37,078 Lakh and Rs. t35,070 Lakh t  nAdjustment for ttttt  nImpact of Fair valuation of Shares &amp; Equity oriented mutual funds Rs. 64,213 Lakh and Rs. 67,840 Lakh  nImpact of Fair Valuation of debt oriented mutual fund Rs. 269 Lakh and Rs. 103 Lakh t  nTax Effect on the above Adjustments Rs. (321) Lakh and Rs. (185) Lakht  nTransferred to non controlling interest Rs. (872)Lakh and Rs. (994) Lakht  nOther equity as reported under Ind AStRs. 1,00,367 Lakh and Rs. 1,01,834 Lakh t  nttt  n6. Effective from 1st April, 2019, the Group has adopted Ind AS 116 Leases. The adoption of the standard did not have any impact on the financial results of the Group.  n  n7. The Board of Directors has recommended, a dividend of Rs. 2.50 per Equity Share of Rs.10/- each for the year ended 31st March, 2020, subject to approval of   nShareholders. t  n  n8. The  figures of current and corresponding quarter are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of the full financial year and the published year to date figures upto the third quarter of the current and corresponding financial year.  nt  n9. The above results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by  the Board of Directors of the Company at their meeting  held on 29th June, 2020 and the Statutory Auditors of the Company have carried out the audit of the same.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfN